# weightsmith configuration. Copy this file to wsp.env at the repo root on each machine that runs
# weightsmith (the GPU host, plus your laptop if you drive the GPU host over ssh), then uncomment
# and edit the lines you need. Every key is shown commented out with its default value.
#
# How the file is read (by weightsmith/config.py and by bin/owsp):
#   - one KEY=VALUE per line. Comments must sit on their own line: anything after the value,
#     including "# ...", becomes part of the value.
#   - the FIRST line for a key wins. Appending a key that is already set further up does nothing.
#   - a variable set in your shell environment wins over this file. A leading ~ is expanded.

# ---- GPU host: where the dependencies live ----------------------------------------------------
# scripts/setup_deps.sh installs these and prints the six lines for your machine. To append them:
#   scripts/setup_deps.sh --print-env >> wsp.env
# If OpenPI, RoboLab and the checkpoint are already installed, point these at your copies instead.
#
# OpenPI fork with request-scoped sampling seeds, and the python of its venv:
# OPENPI_DIR=~/openpi
# OPENPI_PYTHON=~/openpi/.venv/bin/python
# RoboLab checkout (working directory of the simulator; episode outputs go under output/):
# ROBOLAB_DIR=~/robolab
# Isaac Sim / Isaac Lab python with RoboLab installed (also renders frames):
# SIM_PYTHON=~/robolab/.venv/bin/python
# pi0.5 DROID joint-position checkpoint (gs://openpi-assets-simeval/pi05_droid_jointpos):
# CHECKPOINT_DIR=~/.cache/openpi/openpi-assets/checkpoints/pi05_droid_jointpos
# Editable layer-split export of the weights, written once by scripts/prepare_workspace.sh (~11 GB):
# BASE_WORKSPACE=~/weightsmith-workspace/pi05_droid_jointpos-full
# OpenPI download cache (holds the PaliGemma tokenizer):
# OPENPI_DATA_HOME=~/.cache/openpi

# ---- GPU host: GPUs ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One 24 GB GPU: keep the defaults. Everything runs on GPU 0 and per-GPU locks queue the jobs.
# Two GPUs (the reference box has 2x RTX 3090): run evals on GPU 1 and activation captures on
# GPU 0, and let an eval borrow GPU 0 as a second lane whenever it is idle (about 2x faster):
#   WSP_SERVER_GPU=1, WSP_SIM_GPU=1, WSP_ACTS_GPU=0, WSP_EVAL_EXTRA_GPUS=0
#
# GPU of the batched policy server for closed-loop evals:
# WSP_SERVER_GPU=0
# GPU of the Isaac Sim process (16 parallel environments; keep it on the server's GPU):
# WSP_SIM_GPU=0
# GPU of the activation-capture worker (`owsp acts`; loads a second copy of the model, ~9 GB):
# WSP_ACTS_GPU=0
# Extra GPUs an eval may borrow when idle, comma-separated; each runs its own server + Isaac lane:
# WSP_EVAL_EXTRA_GPUS=
# XLA memory fraction of the eval policy server (it shares its GPU with Isaac):
# WSP_SERVER_MEM_FRACTION=0.40
# XLA memory fraction of the capture worker:
# WSP_ACTS_MEM_FRACTION=.9
# Websocket port of the eval policy server; lane i listens on WSP_POOL_PORT+i:
# WSP_POOL_PORT=8300
# Vulkan ICD file for headless Isaac rendering:
# WSP_VK_ICD=/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/nvidia_icd.json

# ---- GPU host: shared locations ---------------------------------------------------------------
# GPU lock files. Every checkout and project on the host must use the same directory, or two
# jobs can land on one GPU at once:
# WSP_LOCK_DIR=~/.cache/weightsmith/locks
# Persistent XLA compilation cache (the first eval and the first capture compile; later ones reuse it):
# WSP_JAX_CACHE=~/.cache/weightsmith/jax
# Policy-server, simulator and pool logs (default: logs/ in this repo):
# WSP_LOG_DIR=
# Operator base-policy surveys (default: survey/ in this repo):
# WSP_SURVEY_DIR=

# ---- Laptop / editor machine: only when you drive the GPU host over ssh -----------------------
# On the GPU host itself leave WSP_HOST unset: bin/owsp then runs everything locally.
#
# ssh host of the GPU box (a name from ~/.ssh/config works):
# WSP_HOST=my-gpu-box
# Path of this repo on the GPU host (absolute, or relative to the remote home directory):
# WSP_REMOTE_REPO=weightsmith
# Python on the GPU host that runs weightsmith/owsp.py (needs numpy):
# WSP_REMOTE_PYTHON=python3
# Where `owsp frames` copies rendered frames (default: ./frames in the current directory):
# WSP_FRAMES_DIR=
# The project root ON THE GPU HOST. Usually set per shell instead: export WSP_ROOT=...
# WSP_ROOT=

# ---- GPU host: tasks kept outside the RoboLab checkout ----------------------------------------
# Directories of extra RoboLab task modules (os.pathsep-separated). A task named by class that one of
# these files defines is loaded from there; the RoboLab checkout itself is never modified. Unset = off.
# Example: the reference-first wording tasks of study/results/sgdw/tasks/.
# WSP_TASK_DIRS=
